  "slug": "neuronal-state-4725",
  "summary": "Three tools automate heterogeneity quantification in cardiomyocyte Ca2+ signals, patient-derived cell calcium traces and neural organoid morphology.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is automated, high-throughput quantification of phenotypic heterogeneity from imaging or signal recordings in stem-cell-derived and patient-derived systems. CardioShift models nested variance to map single-cell Ca2+ transient and contractility distributions in hiPSC-cardiomyocytes. CalDyn, a MATLAB application, automates peak detection, event classification and batch analysis of calcium and electrophysiological signals in patient-derived cells. Organotchi performs brightfield segmentation, ten-feature morphological profiling and longitudinal tracking of neural organoids. What distinguishes the set is the emphasis on open, scalable workflows, with CardioShift adding explicit variance structure. The items do not show cross-system transfer or head-to-head benchmarking of these tools.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-09"
}
